Sift
====

Sift is an independent Linux re-implementation, released under the MIT
license (see LICENSE). It contains no code from the projects below; it
credits them for design and ideas.

Design and product model
------------------------
- Burrow by caezium — https://github.com/caezium/Burrow — MIT License.
  Sift follows Burrow's layout (floating tool rail, Monitor sections, Clean
  hub), its warm espresso/cream palette and per-tool accent colours, and its
  safety model (preview first, reviewed plans, Trash by default, receipts).
  Burrow's engine (burrow-engine, FSL-1.1-ALv2) was NOT copied; Sift's
  engine is written from scratch for Linux.
- Mole (`mo`) by tw93 — https://github.com/tw93/Mole — MIT License.
  The clean / purge / installer / optimize / analyze command model that
  Burrow wraps originates here.
- Squarified treemap layout: Bruls, Huijsen & van Wijk (2000),
  "Squarified Treemaps", re-implemented from the paper.

